-- M4 fixes round 4 (ctxcat r4 id 4): an annotation wrapping the ENTIRE
-- constructor type, telescope included, not just its codomain head.
-- The finding predicted a false Bad_ctor here, on the reading that
-- strip_pis stops at an Ann node the way it stops at Global or Match.
-- It does not: round 1's ctxcat id 8 fix made strip_pis call strip_ann
-- at EVERY level, including the first, so Ann (Pi ...) peels to its
-- binders and the raw result-head walk sees WFoo A x with one index.
-- Executed on the round-3 binary, both spellings already checked, so
-- the finding is REFUTED on behaviour.  This file is the regression
-- pin that was missing: the two spellings, plus an Ann nested INSIDE
-- the telescope on the codomain, all keep checking.  Exact output
-- pinned so a silent re-rejection cannot hide here.
data WFoo (0 A : Type 0) : Nat -> Type 0 :=
  | wmk : ((0 x : Nat) -> WFoo A x : Type 0)
data XFoo (0 A : Type 0) : Nat -> Type 0 :=
  | xmk : (((0 x : Nat) -> XFoo A x) : Type 0)
data YFoo (0 A : Type 0) : Nat -> Type 0 :=
  | ymk : ((0 x : Nat) -> ((YFoo A x) : Type 0) : Type 0)
check WFoo
